    {
      "type": "text",
      "visible": true,
      "sectionLabel": "ABLATION",
      "title": "Split Layer Controls Geometric Decodability",
      "content": {
        "text": "The split layer $L_s$ determines whether predicted tokens can become usable 3D structure. The best split is $L_s=12$, where shallow GFM layers have extracted enough visual structure and deep GFM layers still have enough capacity to decode future geometry.\n\nWhen the predictor is inserted too early, the tokens are under-formed. When it is inserted too late, the remaining GFM blocks cannot integrate predicted future tokens into the pretrained geometric prior."
      },
      "id": "d581c54c"
    },
